253:  // When THIS user agreed to have their results ranked in THIS tournament.
254:  //
255:  // Lives here, not on tournament_participants, because ELO is applied per
256:  // tournament_rosters.userId: a team participant can carry several users
257:  // (MAIN + RESERVE), so a single per-participant timestamp cannot tell whose
258:  // consent it is — one user confirming would hand every team-mate their score.
259:  //
260:  // NULL means not confirmed. Distinct from tournament_participants.ranking_consent,
261:  // which is only a copy of the tournament's isRanked flag.
262:  //
263:  // Business rule: a match counts only when matches.completedAt >= this instant.
264:  // Matches played before confirming stay permanently unscored, so nobody can be
265:  // force-enrolled and then have old results land against them.
266:  rankingConsentAt: timestamp('ranking_consent_at', { withTimezone: true }),
267:  joinedAt: timestamp('joined_at', { withTimezone: true })
268:    .defaultNow()
269:    .notNull(),
270:  // When the confirmation mail was last queued, and how many times it has been
271:  // sent. Self-reminders (1-3, then stop) are scheduled from these — without them
272:  // the scheduler cannot tell "never notified" from "notified and ignored", and
273:  // the organizer's "awaiting confirmation" view becomes unverifiable.
